  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point is $5$ units to the *left* of the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $-5.$\n\nAdditionally, the point is $7$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has a $y$-coordinate of $-7.$\n\nThe point has an $x$-coordinate of $-5$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-7,$ so its coordinates are $(-5,-7).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
